/*  The model: what a playing field is made of.

    ★★ No wrapper, no marker, no pull. This file is in `tools/snake/`, so what it declares belongs
    to the namespace `snake` along with everything its neighbours declare — the directory says
    what an `and book` used to have to say a second time. A book or a module inside a project is
    still perfectly legal; there is just nothing left for one to do here.

    ⚠ Nothing here draws anything or reads a key. The model knows where things are and what counts
    as the same square; the view knows how that looks and the controller knows what a keypress
    means. Keeping them apart is the point of the exercise as much as the game is.
*/

/// One square of the playing field, counted from 1 at the top left.
Define object spot with (the number row, the number column):

    /// Whether two squares are the same square.
    Bind fact to same-as, given (the spot other):
        Return one's row is other's row and one's column is other's column.
    Done.
Done.

/// How many rows the field has.
Bind number to height:
    Return 8.
Done.

/// How many columns the field has.
Bind number to width:
    Return 20.
Done.

/// A square, from its coordinates.
Bind spot to at, given (the number row, the number column):
    Return a new spot { the row row, the column column }.
Done.

/// Whether a square is still on the field.
Bind fact to holds, given (the spot which):
    Return which's row is not less than 1
       and which's row is not greater than cast height
       and which's column is not less than 1
       and which's column is not greater than cast width.
Done.
